{
  "_provenance": {
    "capturedFrom": "isolated throwaway `opencode serve` on 127.0.0.1:4792 with its own XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_DATA_HOME, so the session-state plugin was NOT loaded and no live overlay was touched",
    "opencodeVersion": "1.17.13",
    "capturedAt": "2026-07-31",
    "how": "global config {\"permission\":\"ask\"} forces a real bash permission prompt. Two sessions were created in two different directories on the SAME serve; one was driven with claude-haiku-4-5 until it called the bash tool. The five directory queries were then issued back-to-back against that single pending prompt, and RAW response bodies recorded. The prompt was then replied to via POST /permission/{requestID}/reply, capturing a genuinely MATCHED permission.asked -> permission.replied pair from the SSE stream.",
    "why": "Closes carried-forward Task 3 review gaps: the GET response shape behind fetchPendingSnapshot was never verified against a deployed server holding a real pending prompt, and the .asked/.replied key asymmetry was only ever confirmed for question.*, never permission.*.",
    "liveOverlayTripwire": "listing of ~/.local/share/opencode/session-state.d identical before and after",
    "note": "Raw bodies are stored, not hand-recorded counts, so the tests derive counts and id membership from real data rather than trusting a transcription. The final unfiltered repeat is a temporal control proving the prompt was still pending for the whole sequence, so the zero counts are filtering and not a mid-sequence reply."
  },
